---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout title="Studio Guide">
  <main class="guide-container">
    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="kicker">Owner’s Manual</span>
      <h1>Running Your Studio &amp; Gallery</h1>
      <p>
        Everything on your site is managed from your phone or laptop through{' '}
        <a href="https://app.pagescms.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pages CMS</a>—no code or
        terminal required. Whenever you hit <strong>Save</strong>, the site updates automatically in
        about 45 seconds.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2>1. How Your Four Gallery Sections Work</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        When you create or edit an entry under <strong>Works &amp; Finds</strong> in Pages CMS, the{' '}
        <strong>Gallery Section</strong> dropdown decides where it lives on the homepage:
      </p>

      <div class="room-grid">
        <div class="room-card">
          <span class="room-tag">For Sale • Curated</span>
          <h3>Quality Finds</h3>
          <p>
            Vintage furniture, estate pieces, and salvaged objects you restore or curate for sale.
            Set Availability to <strong>Available</strong> and add a price so it appears under both{' '}
            <em>For Sale</em> and <em>Quality Finds</em>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="room-card">
          <span class="room-tag">For Sale • Studio Work</span>
          <h3>Originals for Sale</h3>
          <p>
            Your own sculptures, articulated dolls, paintings, and one-of-a-kind works available to
            collectors. Visitors can click any piece to inspect full notes, dimensions, and inquire
            or purchase.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="room-card">
          <span class="room-tag">Personal Curation</span>
          <h3>Collection</h3>
          <p>
            Objects, ceramics, and reference pieces you collect and live with in the studio—not for
            sale. Set Availability to <strong>Not for Sale</strong> so price tags and inquiry buttons
            stay hidden.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="room-card">
          <span class="room-tag">Body of Work</span>
          <h3>Original Archive</h3>
          <p>
            Past original works, studies, and sold pieces you want to document as part of your
            ongoing portfolio. Mark sold works as <strong>Sold</strong> to display a quiet{' '}
            <em>Sold</em> label.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2>2. Posting a New Piece from Your Phone</h2>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li>
          Open <a href="https://app.pagescms.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">app.pagescms.org</a>{' '}
          and select <strong>shop-sachie</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap <strong>Works &amp; Finds</strong>, then tap <strong>New Entry</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Upload your <strong>Primary Photograph</strong> straight from your camera roll, plus any
          detail angles or before-and-after shots under <strong>Detail &amp; Alternate Views</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Choose the <strong>Gallery Section</strong>, <strong>Availability</strong>, and{' '}
          <strong>Medium</strong>, then fill in dimensions, materials, and your curatorial notes.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap <strong>Save</strong>. Your live gallery rebuilds automatically in under a minute.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2>3. Using Your Private Studio Desk (<a href={`${base}/studio`}>/studio</a>)</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Your <a href={`${base}/studio`}>Studio Desk</a> is a working back-office page for tracking
        numbers and cross-posting items without cluttering your public gallery:
      </p>

      <div class="two-col">
        <div class="info-box">
          <h3>Sales &amp; Studio Ledger</h3>
          <p>
            Each entry has two optional number fields in Pages CMS that never appear on the public
            gallery cards:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Private Studio Spend ($):</strong> What you paid to acquire a piece plus
              restoration or art materials.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Private Final Sale Amount ($):</strong> What the piece actually sold for once
              Availability is switched to <strong>Sold</strong>.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Your <a href={`${base}/studio`}>Studio Desk</a> automatically totals your{' '}
            <strong>Gross Sales</strong>, <strong>Total Studio Spend</strong>, and{' '}
            <strong>Net Balance</strong> across every piece.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-box">
          <h3>External Listing Prep (eBay &amp; Marketplace)</h3>
          <p>
            Every item marked <strong>Available</strong> under <em>Quality Finds</em> or{' '}
            <em>Originals for Sale</em> automatically generates ready-to-paste copy on your{' '}
            <a href={`${base}/studio`}>Studio Desk</a>:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>eBay Title &amp; Description:</strong> Pre-trimmed to eBay’s 80-character
              title limit with provenance, dimensions, and condition notes formatted cleanly.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Facebook Marketplace / Local:</strong> Clean local-buyer post with pickup
              notes and dimensions up front, plus a <strong>Download Photo</strong> link.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2>4. Updating Your Bio, Contact Info, or Palette</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Open <strong>Studio Settings</strong> inside Pages CMS to update your artist statement,
        contact email, Instagram handle, or background and accent hex tones at any time.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-container {
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.75rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }
  .guide-header {
    padding-bottom: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .kicker {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .guide-header h1 {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 2.35rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .guide-header p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 680px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }
  .guide-header a,
  .guide-section a {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .guide-section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }
  .guide-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.65rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .section-intro {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .room-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .room-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .room-card,
  .info-box {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .room-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  .room-card h3,
  .info-box h3 {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .room-card p,
  .info-box p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #d4d1ca;
  }
  .room-card p:last-child,
  .info-box p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .step-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: #dcd9d2;
  }
  .step-list li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 740px) {
    .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .info-box ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: #d4d1ca;
  }
</style>
